.TH U-CONFIG 1 2024-08-22 u-config
.
.SH NAME
u-config \- smaller, simpler, portable pkg-config clone
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B u-config
.RI [ options ]
.I package
.RI [ package " ...]"
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B u-config
is a small, highly portable pkg-config and pkgconf clone.
It retrieves compiler and linker flags, version, and other dependency
information of software packages.
.PP
Package metadata is retrieved from
.RB \(lq .pc \(rq
text files, located in a system-specific path.
You can override the default search path with environment variables like
.BR PKG_CONFIG_PATH .
See
.B ENVIRONMENT
for more information.
.PP
This manual page describes the
.B u-config
utility in particular.
For general information about pkg-config concepts and its file format,
refer to manual pages provided by other projects, like
.BR pkgconf (1)
and
.BR pc (5).
.PP
.B u-config
supports a subset of the options of other pkg-config implementations.
For a list of supported options, use the
.B \-\-help
option.
Some of them are unique to
.BR u-config :
.TP
.B \-\-newlines
Separate arguments by line feeds instead of spaces, which is sometimes
useful like in the fish shell or when manually examining output.
.TP
.B \-\-msvc\-syntax
Translates and prints compiler arguments into a syntax compatible with the
MSVC compiler.
For example,
.BI \-l " libname"
becomes
.BR libname.lib .
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.B u-config
supports all the important pkg-config run-time environment variables.
To see which are supported, use the
.B \-\-help
option.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
$ u-config \-\-cflags \-\-libs foo
\-I/usr/include/foo \-DFOO_HAS_BAR=1 \-lfoo
.fi
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgconf (1),
.BR pc (5)
.
